answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323189}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "695450ef-6209-5a8e-874a-0e67f88a5889" :question/math-academy-id "q-38076" :question/problem "![](images/bc/bccbe3973fa63908f5e264f4566e1207c5019dc1de9c36ef42481428527aef3b.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the semicircle shown above. What is\n${∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A$\nexpressed in polar coordinates?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $2$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}2(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278358 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d298631-2765-5ac2-b97f-679ad8916a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276009} {:answer/id #uuid "40abc3c2-e544-59b8-9c14-f0e4a01c790c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276041} {:answer/id #uuid "97eed52a-8abb-5db8-9604-798e79ac4216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{r}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276843} {:answer/id #uuid "9c39af7e-789b-5aed-9430-612b825a204f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276878} {:answer/id #uuid "b24b07d6-5486-598f-99db-263fe3587090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{2}{e}^{r}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c39af7e-789b-5aed-9430-612b825a204f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276878} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fde4879-96cb-5c11-ab63-d504fc117051" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277857}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ebe3923c-2578-5c4c-8b9f-d97199b48c08" :question/math-academy-id "q-161038" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa5b04b98d3796656fca912d8dc1732ea7e12bab9083f8ca543ad5fd4fdb10ff.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the quarter-circle shown above. What is ${∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ expressed in polar coordinates?" :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $4$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4,\\,\\pi \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}{e}^{(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{4}r{e}^{{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "386528aa-7c36-5737-95bd-6ec28d6f21f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275976} {:answer/id #uuid "49aae471-6334-5b21-a65c-5f8c10050325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276128} {:answer/id #uuid "55731809-fff3-5c19-92fe-0dfc9e836434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276236} {:answer/id #uuid "baa1523e-3758-588f-a054-6103cf0c3a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277133} {:answer/id #uuid "f26af378-506e-5ab0-a93f-58cf9b6e8e19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baa1523e-3758-588f-a054-6103cf0c3a32" :a